# The input rail. Colang 1.0.
#
# `execute` runs the system action jamjet_guardrails_check_input, which returns
# false for a deny and true for an allow or a redact. A redact has already
# replaced $user_message by the time this flow reads $allowed, so there is
# nothing for the flow to do about it: the rewritten message is what the rest of
# the turn sees.
#
# `bot refuse to respond` is deliberately NOT defined here. It is the name NeMo's
# own rails use, so a config that already defines it gets its own wording, and a
# definition shipped in this file would silently replace it. A config that
# enables this flow must define one; the package README gives the line.

define flow jamjet guardrails check input
  $allowed = execute jamjet_guardrails_check_input

  if not $allowed
    bot refuse to respond
    stop
